Olive Oil Cake
  --Suzy Karadsheh

1 cup evoo, fruity, more neutral-tasting, plus extra for the pan
2 c ap flour + more for the pan
1 tsp kosher salt
1 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
3/4 - 1 tsp ground cardamom
1 1/2 c + 2 tbsp sugar
3 large eggs
grated zest of 2 oranges + 2 tbsp fresh orange juice
1 1/4 c whole milk or plant-based alternative
2 tbsp sifted confectioners’ sugar, for garnish

Position a rack in the center of the oven and preheat the oven to 350F. Brush the bottom and sides of a 9" round cake pan with a little olive oil. Line the bottom of the pan with a round of parchment paper and dust with a bit of the flour, shaking out the excess. In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, salt, baking powder, and baking soda. In a large bowl, combine the 1 1/2 c sugar, cardamom, and eggs. Using an electric hand mixer set on high, beat the mixture until thick and fluffy, ~5 min (or use a stand mixer on high speed). While the mixer is running, slowly drizzle in the olive oil and beat until incorporated. Reduce the speed to low and add half the orange zest, the orange juice, and milk. Beat until smooth. Add the flour mixture to wet ingredients and mix on low just until you have a uniform batter. Pour the cake batter into the pan and sprinkle the top with the remaining 2 tbsp sugar. Bake the cake for 40-45 min, or until the center is set and a skewer inserted into the middle comes out clean (ovens do vary, so check your cake at 30 min and go from there). Allow the cake to cool for 30 min in the pan, then run a small knife around the edge, invert the cake onto a large plate, then invert again onto a rack to cool completely. Before serving, dust the cake with powdered sugar and sprinkle with orange zest.
